# Paid PDF fulfillment (Stripe + Vercel)

## API routes

| Route | Role |
|-------|------|
| `api/stripe-webhook.js` | Verify signature → `fulfillCheckoutSession()` |
| `api/_lib/fulfillment.js` | Redis state, Resend email, signed tokens, PDF fetch |
| `api/download.js` | Long-lived (7-day) signed PDF — email link |
| `api/download-link.js` | Short-lived (15-min) URL by `session_id` — `success.html` poll |
| `api/fulfillment-health.js` | Production env + Redis / Stripe / Blob config probe |

## Golden rule (same production host)

Payment Link **success URL**, Stripe **webhook URL**, Upstash Redis, and Vercel **Production env** must all target the **same** buyer-facing domain (e.g. `promptanatomy.online`).

**Anti-pattern:** webhook on `promptanatomy.app` while buyers land on `promptanatomy.online` → webhook returns 200 but `success.html` shows “session not found”. See [`todo.md`](../../todo.md) §1b and [`memo_pdf.md`](../../memo_pdf.md).

## Environment (all or nothing)

Required set, shared by `api/_lib/fulfillment.js`, `/api/fulfillment-health`, `scripts/check-fulfillment-env.js`, and `DEPLOY.md`: `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `STRIPE_PRICE_*_PDF`, Upstash URL/token, `DOWNLOAD_TOKEN_SECRET`, `RESEND_API_KEY`, `FULFILLMENT_FROM_EMAIL`, `PDF_*_SOURCE_URL`, `BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN`, `SITE_URL`.

Checklists: [`memo_pdf.md`](../../memo_pdf.md) §3, [`DEPLOY.md`](../../DEPLOY.md).

`STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` must work for `sessions.retrieve` — signature verification alone is insufficient.

## Product mapping (priority)

1. Payment Link `metadata.product` = `beginners` | `advanced`
2. `STRIPE_PRICE_*` env ids
3. `amount_total` fallback (499 / 999 cents)

Do not rely on amount alone in production.

## Diagnostics

- `GET /api/fulfillment-health` → `{ ok, missing, redis, blobConfigured, stripeConfigured, priceMappingConfigured, siteUrlConfigured }`
- Webhook 500 responses include `detail` for Stripe Dashboard
- After env fix: **replay** `checkout.session.completed` in Stripe (do not re-charge buyer)

## Before deploy / after incident

```bash
npm test
npm run check:fulfillment   # local Redis + optional checks
```

Production: DEPLOY post-deploy checklist + [`todo.md`](../../todo.md) P0 §2 (test-mode purchase + refund).

## Tests

- Structure asserts: fulfillment helpers, health route, env validation hooks
- E2E: success-page poll with mocked `/api/download-link` in [`tests/e2e/core-flow.spec.js`](../../tests/e2e/core-flow.spec.js)

Do not change fulfillment without running `npm test`; recommend full `test:mixed` before release.
